3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.630
She was recognized by "Good Housekeeping"

4
00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.190
as an interior designer who is changing the world.

5
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.860
She's the contributing editor

6
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.290
of "House Beautiful", my favorite,

7
00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.090
and the founder of Kingston Design Connection.

8
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.280
Please welcome interior designer extraordinaire

9
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.491
Maryline Damour.

10
00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:24.680
(audience applauding)

11
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.513
Hi.

12
00:00:26.821 --> 00:00:28.050
Thank you so much for having me on.

13
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:28.950
I can't believe I'm here.

14
00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.180
Oh my God, I'm so honored.

15
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.890
You are really one of my favorite designers.

16
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.440
I follow everything you do.

17
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.540
What is your biggest design tip?

18
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.150
What's budget friendly design advice?

19
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.930
You know, this is something I tell my clients

20
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:47.930 line:15%
all the time that the simplest thing to do is plan ahead.

21
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.730 line:15%
And we do this as interior designers all the time

22
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:53.310
in terms of developing mood boards and renderings.

23
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.190
'Cause at the end of the day,

24
00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:57.280
you can change anything on papers as many times as you want

25
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.340
and something as even inexpensive as paint,

26
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.488
if you need to repaint,

27
00:01:01.488 --> 00:01:03.770
that can get pretty costly pretty quickly.

28
00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:06.560
So taking the time to do all of that stuff on paper

29
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.700
means that when you're ready to go,

30
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.240
there are fewer missteps.

31
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.790
All right, well, we're having a new homeowner

32
00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.810
with her design dilemma, a few upgrades that are under $30.

33
00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.610
Let's take a look!

34
00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:18.070 line:15%
Hi, Drew. My name is Julie.

35
00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.590 line:15%
I live in Brewster, New York

36
00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.500
with my husband and two small boys.

37
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.530
About seven months ago,

38
00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.260
we bought our new house and we need help.

39
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:28.670
The previous owners gifted us this hutch and dining set,

40
00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.810
and although it's beautiful, it's just really not our style

41
00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.920
and it doesn't work for us in this room.

42
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.170
I would love to get rid of the hutch

43
00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.320
except then it leaves this huge blank wall

44
00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.460
that I do not know what to do with.

45
00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.640
Do you have any tips that could help me maximize the space?

46
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.810
Please help us. We'd be so grateful. Thank you.

47
00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.032
Please welcome, Julie Miller!

48
00:01:50.032 --> 00:01:52.859
(audience applauding)

49
00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:54.441
Thank you for coming on the show.

50
00:01:54.441 --> 00:01:56.294
Oh my God, this is great.
Okay.

51
00:01:56.294 --> 00:02:01.140
So Maryline, take us through your suggestions, your insight.

52
00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.900
I wanna hear everything. So I'm putting it over to you.

53
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.650
So one of the first things that I did

54
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.450
was to find a lovely floral wallpaper.

55
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.490
So that way your dining room

56
00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.630 line:15%
can be surrounded in springtime.

57
00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.240 line:15%
And we definitely got rid of the hutch.

58
00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.073 line:15%
Okay.
But we wanted you

59
00:02:15.073 --> 00:02:16.990 line:15%
to keep the storage that you had,

60
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.400 line:15%
so we brought in these lovely floating shelves.

61
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.750
This is stunning.

62
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.960 line:15%
And you can see that you can mix them up.

63
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.400 line:15%
It can be shelving for your dinnerware

64
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.170
as well as books, et cetera.

65
00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.480 line:15%
And we framed it out in lovely framing.

66
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.687 line:15%
And you have two children, I understand.

67
00:02:32.687 --> 00:02:33.790 line:15%
I do. Toddler.

68
00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.740 line:15%
(Julie and Maryline laughs)

69
00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.020
It's crazy.
Yep.

70
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:37.853
Crazy time.

71
00:02:37.853 --> 00:02:42.170
I think we should, as a society, agree, it's a buckle up.

72
00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.003
Absolutely.

73
00:02:43.003 --> 00:02:45.000
You know, so I'm definitely have the mindset

74
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.570
that we should be creating children's spaces in our homes.

75
00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.790
And even if it's an elegant space,

76
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.520 line:15%
there's an elegant way to include children in our homes.

77
00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.130 line:15%
So one of the ways that I did that

78
00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.591 line:15%
was to bring in a chalkboard at children level.

79
00:02:57.591 --> 00:02:58.760 line:15%
I love this. Oh my God.

80
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.360 line:15%
And as you can see... (audience applauding)

81
00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.588
Yes, it's so good!

82
00:03:03.588 --> 00:03:05.240
Julie, do you like...

83
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.073
How do you feel?

84
00:03:06.073 --> 00:03:07.450
Ah, I'm dying. Oh my God.

85
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.520
This is just...

86
00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.410
And to cook a meal,

87
00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.940
like your kids can color while you cook a meal

88
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.520
and not on your table, they can color on this chalkboard.

89
00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.580
I love a good game of tic-tac-toe too.

90
00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:17.413
I know.

91
00:03:17.413 --> 00:03:18.246
All right.

92
00:03:18.246 --> 00:03:20.310
What is your vision for the dining table set?

93
00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:21.700
What did you do here?

94
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.950
So your dining table and chair set were dark wood

95
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:25.783
all of it.
Yes.

96
00:03:25.783 --> 00:03:28.040
Right. So we actually lightened it up.

97
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.880 line:15%
So that way, your space is light and bright and airy.

98
00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.120 line:15%
And so one of the ways we did that

99
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.090 line:15%
was through these slip covers.

100
00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.150
I don't know why I didn't think of this.

101
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.230
Yeah. And since you-
I needed you.

102
00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.310 line:15%
Yeah, since you have children,

103
00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.840 line:15%
it's easy to swap them out,

104
00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.010 line:15%
throw them in the washing machine.

105
00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.940 line:15%
Maryline, can you buy pre-made slip covers

106
00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.160
that kind of generically fit a chair,

107
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.700
if you will.
Yes. Absolutely.

108
00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:51.350
Well, Julie, what do you think?

109
00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.440
I'm so in love. Oh my gosh.
Really?

110
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.549
It is like, so...

111
00:03:56.549 --> 00:03:59.140
It is so beautiful. Oh my God.

112
00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.970
It is everything. The table...

113
00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.320
Oh my God. My Pinterest. This is my Pinterest.

114
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.470
One thing I wanna point out

115
00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.390 line:15%
that we're talking about all throughout the week

116
00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.950 line:15%
that has definitely influenced me as of late as well,

117
00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:12.830 line:15%
is the pops of black.

118
00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.203
I think it's really kind of rising to the top.

119
00:04:15.203 --> 00:04:16.036
Yeah.

120
00:04:16.036 --> 00:04:18.970
Of a really great way to minimalistically,

121
00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:23.032
or as a maximalist, really chic up your space.

122
00:04:23.032 --> 00:04:24.184
(audience applauding)

123
00:04:24.184 --> 00:04:25.800
Yeah, absolutely.
Come on.

124
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.040
Well, I'm so glad you like it 'cause guess what?

125
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.700
You're getting everything.

126
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:30.533
Oh my God.

127
00:04:30.533 --> 00:04:32.206
All of these is going home with you.

128
00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:34.260
(audience applauding)

129
00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.280
Oh my God.

130
00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.430
And we're gonna give you $500

131
00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.620
to just get it installed, make it all happen.

132
00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.453
Oh my God.

133
00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:43.590
Bibbidi-boo. Just everything dialed in.

134
00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.067
Thank you so much.
Of course, Julie.

135
00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.650 line:15%
(upbeat music)

